course: dictionary
lesson: 7673
title: Proportional: the right size compared with something else
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: «Proportional» describes two things that are linked by a fixed rule, so that when one changes, the other changes in the same way. In maths, if one pencil costs 20p, then five pencils cost 100p, because 100 is always five times 20.
explain: «Proportional representation is a different system in which a party's share of seats matches its share of votes.» Here proportional means fair in size: a party with about a quarter of the votes gets about a quarter of the seats.
explain: Use the clue words around it. «New Zealand uses MMP (mixed-member proportional)» tells you the word is describing a system, and the rest of the sentence explains how it works. Ask yourself: proportional to what? The answer is the thing being compared.
fact: Proportional means having the right size or amount compared with something else.
fact: In maths, two amounts are proportional if one is always the same number times the other.
fact: Common phrases include «directly proportional», «inversely proportional», «proportional to» and «proportional representation».
fact: In «proportional representation», parties get seats in proportion to their votes.
fact: When amounts are directly proportional, a graph of them is a straight line through zero.
exercise: If 1 pencil costs 20p, what does 5 pencils cost when the cost is proportional to the number of pencils? | 25p | *100p | 50p | 200p
exercise: «Proportional representation is a different system in which a party's share of seats matches its share of votes.» In this sentence, proportional means | Only for big parties | *Fair in size, matching the votes | Quick and simple | Very large
exercise: «New Zealand uses MMP (mixed-member proportional).» Which words are the full name of MMP? | *mixed-member proportional | mixed-member popular | money-making party | main-member proportional
test: Lily says a punishment should be proportional to the wrong done. What does this mean? | It should only be given in winter | It should be the same for every wrong, however small | *It should be fair in size compared with the wrong done | It should be the biggest possible, whatever the wrong
test: A recipe for 2 people needs 100g of flour. If the amounts are proportional, how much flour does a recipe for 4 people need? | 150g | *200g | 400g | 50g
exam: Which of these best describes proportional? | *Having the right size or amount compared with something else | Very noisy and loud | A kind of fruit | Always equal to zero
